+/*!
+   \fn bool QCborStreamReader::isNumber() const
+   \since 6.13
+
+   Returns true if the type of the current element is a number: an unsigned
+   or negative integer, or an IEEE 754 half-, single- or double-precision
+   floating point (that is, if isInteger(), isFloat16(), isFloat() or
+   isDouble() returns true). If this function returns true, you may call
+   toNumber() to read the value as a \c double.
+
+   Note that this function returns false for CBOR tags, even those that wrap
+   numeric content (such as QCborKnownTags::PositiveBignum or
+   QCborKnownTags::Decimal), and for simple types, including booleans.
+
+   \sa type(), toNumber(), isInteger(), isFloat16(), isFloat(), isDouble()
+ */
